# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect syntax.
#
# security.txt has to live at /security.txt on this host (its file manager
# won't create a directory whose name starts with a dot), but the spec
# (RFC 9116 §4) expects it at /.well-known/security.txt. A redirect from the
# spec path to the real file is explicitly the mechanism the RFC anticipates
# for exactly this situation — this is not a workaround, it's the documented
# way to publish the file from a location that can't hold the dot-directory.
#
# 200 here means "rewrite", not "redirect": the browser's address bar and any
# automated RFC 9116 fetcher both see content at /.well-known/security.txt,
# with no visible bounce to /security.txt.
/.well-known/security.txt   /security.txt   200
